.TH TGLFS-UPLOAD 1 "March 2026" "tglfs 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tglfs-upload \- upload one file, or archive multiple files, into Telegram Saved Messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tglfs upload
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIpaths...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uploads one file directly into Saved Messages, or packages multiple files into a tar archive using the same naming convention as the web app before uploading.
.PP
New uploads use file-card protocol v5 with independently compressed and authenticated encrypted blocks. Multi-file batches and individual .tar files include an encrypted member directory. Other archive formats remain ordinary files.
.PP
Repeat the command with the original files and password to resume completed blocks without rereading or recompressing them. The initial source scan records hashes and UFID in an encrypted upload plan. Keep input files unchanged until completion. Interrupted transfer records remain in Telegram; passwords and keys are not stored in checkpoints.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-interactive
Disable interactive prompts and fail instead of prompting.
.TP
.B --password <password>
Encryption password.
.TP
.B --password-env [name]
Read the encryption password from an environment variable. If no name is provided, the command uses
.B TGLFS_UPLOAD_PASSWORD.
.TP
.B --password-stdin
Read the encryption password from standard input.
.TP
.B --resume <id>
Resume one specific upload session. A mismatched source or password is refused.
.TP
.B --json
Emit machine-readable JSON.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TGLFS_UPLOAD_PASSWORD
Default environment variable for the upload encryption password.
.SH AI AGENT NOTES
TTY uploads render separate UFID and upload progress bars.
.B --json
prints exactly one final JSON object to standard output, writes failures to standard error, and never prompts. If no password source is supplied, the password is the empty string. The same encryption process is used, but an empty password provides no password-based confidentiality.
